# Every text file here is committed LF, on every platform. This makes a working
# copy agree with that, and it is not a style preference.
#
# gofmt is the sharp case. It rewrites CRLF and then reports the file as
# unformatted, so on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true `gofmt -l .` —
# which AGENTS.md requires to print nothing — listed 57 files whose committed
# content is perfectly formatted. The diff it wanted was the carriage returns
# and nothing else. Nobody had broken the formatting; the working copy simply
# did not match the index, and the check could not be run at all.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` on its own: auto leaves the ending to
# core.autocrlf, which is the setting that caused this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# No line endings to normalise, and a normalised one is a corrupted one. Fonts
# are the only binaries committed today; the rest are here so that adding a
# screenshot to the docs cannot quietly mangle it.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff   binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
